 IMPORTANT NOTE: THERE IS NO SOLICITATION AVAILABLE AT THIS TIME. REQUESTS FOR A SOLICITATION WILL NOT RECEIVE A RESPONSE. 

 This Request for Information (RFI) is in support of Market Research being conducted by the United States Census Bureau (USCB) to gather general information and explore potential available solutions to support the agency&rsquo;s need. This is  not  a Request for Proposal/Request for Quote or an indication that a contractual commitment will exist for this requirement. The Government does not intend to award a contract solely on the basis of this market research. No funds are necessarily obligated for any requirement or solicitation that may or may not ultimately arise from the results of this market research. 



 The purpose of this tentative requirement is to promptly onboard expertise to support the Regional and Decennial infrastructure required to conduct large scale, time sensitive field operations. This includes the technical support needed to implement new training for Field operations and the systems that support hiring, training, pay and data collection efforts and the resulting analysis. 

 This contract vehicle will provide support for current surveys, Decennial Census data collection, and geographic operations, including pre-2030 Decennial Census tests and objectives. 
&nbsp;&nbsp; &nbsp; 
&nbsp;A large portion of the support to assist in opening over 90 temporary offices from which hiring, training, coordinating material distribution, data collection, and payroll efforts will be administered or managed. &nbsp;Securing those office leases requires multiple staff with the knowledge and expertise to negotiate and secure lease and equipment agreements, Federal Protective Services, HVAC needs, space buildout, supplies, electrical, and network setup, this includes receiving equipment deliveries, setting up, and managing these temporary spaces the same as our permanent government spaces. Ultimately, Field Division must dismantle the infrastructure and release staff as promptly as they were secured. Contractual support staff are ideal for these monumental efforts. 
&nbsp;&nbsp; &nbsp; 
The services will be provided via the issuance of fixed price, time and material, or a combination of both call order types will enable FLD to obtain contractual support for divisions and program offices at Headquarters (HQ) to support the Census mission. The Contractor shall provide the services listed in Task Area 1 through 17 under Agreement Requirements. &nbsp;These Task Areas include but are not limited to; assisting in technical and operational writing, automated training development, infrastructure, recruiting, space planning, personnel and payroll, training development, training delivery, scheduling, training support, help desk support, SharePoint support, database engineering and administration, analytical and quantitative analysis. 
&nbsp;
